# Lesson 5, new exercise: opener shows hearts, then declines an invitation.
title: Hearts, and a minimum
id: L05-09
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.2, 5.6
student: S
board: 18
dealer: E
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  A2     T754   KJ84   654
  E  KQ643  82     A976   83
  S  T95    AKQ6   Q32    AT2
  W  J87    J93    T5     KQJ97

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1NT*   = 15-17 points, balanced
     not *: 15 points and a balanced hand: open 1NT.
  W Pass
  N 2C     = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
  E Pass
  S 2H*    = Four hearts
     key: Four hearts, so bid 2♥.
     not 2D: 2♦ says "no 4-card major." You have four hearts.
  W Pass
  N 3H     = Four hearts too, 8-9 points: invitational
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = A minimum: decline
     key: 15 is a minimum, so decline the invitation.
     not 4H: 3♥ invites. With a minimum, say no.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  You showed four hearts, and North raised to 3♥: four hearts and 8-9 points,
  inviting game. With 15, a minimum, you passed. South is declarer, because
  South bid hearts first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 5
  remind: What is the contract?

play:
  1   W CK  N C4  E C3  S CA
  2   S HA*  W H3  N H4  E H2
      HA key: Draw trumps first, with your top hearts.
      HA not H6: Did you remember that your top trumps can draw the opponents' trumps?
      note: Draw trumps.
  3   S HK  W H9  N H5  E H8
      note: Keep drawing trumps.
  4   S HQ  W HJ  N H7  E S3
      note: Trumps are drawn.
  5   S ST  W S7  N S2  E SQ
      note: Trumps are drawn. Lead a spade toward dummy's ace.
  6   E DA  S D2  W D5  N D4
  7   E C8  S C2  W C9  N C5
  8   W CQ  N C6  E S4  S CT
  9   W CJ  N HT  E S6  S D3
      note: Dummy ruffs.
  10  N DK  E D6  S DQ  W DT
      note: Now the diamonds, to set up dummy's winners.
  11  N DJ  E D7  S S5  W C7
      note: Cash dummy's good diamond.
  12  N SA  E SK  S S9  W S8
      note: Cash the ace of spades.
  13  N D8  E D9  S H6  W SJ
      note: 9 tricks: 3♥ made.

play recap:
  The plan: draw trumps, then ruff a club loser in dummy and use dummy's
  diamonds. Drawing trumps with your top hearts comes first, so the defense
  can't ruff your winners.

  3♥ made exactly. 4♥ would have gone down one. With a minimum opposite an
  invitation, passing was right, and this time it was rewarded.
